        "answer": {
          "short": "$10$\n\nSimplify and square $x+\\frac{1}{x}$, then subtract $2$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{1}{x}&=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{2}}\\\\\\frac{1}{x}&=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{2}}{3-2}\\\\\\frac{1}{x}&=\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{2}\\\\x+\\frac{1}{x}&=(\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{2})+(\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{2})\\\\x+\\frac{1}{x}&=2\\sqrt{3}\\end{align*}$$\n\nSquaring the sum gives a cross term of $2x\\cdot\\frac{1}{x}=2$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}x^2+\\frac{1}{x^2}&=\\left(x+\\frac{1}{x}\\right)^2-2\\\\x^2+\\frac{1}{x^2}&=(2\\sqrt{3})^2-2\\\\x^2+\\frac{1}{x^2}&=10\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 42
      },
      {
        "id": "p10-q9-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Use a similar technique to calculate $x^2-\\frac{1}{x^2}$, if $x=-2+\\sqrt{5}$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-8\\sqrt{5}$\n\nMultiply the simplified difference $x-\\frac{1}{x}$ by the simplified sum $x+\\frac{1}{x}$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{1}{x}&=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}-2}\\\\\\frac{1}{x}&=\\frac{\\sqrt{5}+2}{5-4}\\\\\\frac{1}{x}&=\\sqrt{5}+2\\\\x-\\frac{1}{x}&=(\\sqrt{5}-2)-(\\sqrt{5}+2)=-4\\\\x+\\frac{1}{x}&=(\\sqrt{5}-2)+(\\sqrt{5}+2)=2\\sqrt{5}\\end{align*}$$\n\n$$\\begin{align*}x^2-\\frac{1}{x^2}&=\\left(x-\\frac{1}{x}\\right)\\left(x+\\frac{1}{x}\\right)\\\\x^2-\\frac{1}{x^2}&=(-4)(2\\sqrt{5})\\\\x^2-\\frac{1}{x^2}&=-8\\sqrt{5}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 38
      }
    ]
